  <section class="mission-hero">
    <div class="mission-hero-inner">
      <a class="back-link" href="/missions">&larr; All missions</a>
      <div class="mission-category">Event · Barcelona</div>
      <h1>Marine Technology &amp; Innovation Forum 2026</h1>
      <p class="mission-lead">An evening at IAAC where students, researchers, partners and industry shared their work on marine technology and robotics.</p>
      <dl class="mission-facts">
        <div><dt>Date</dt><dd>21 May 2026, 18:30</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Venue</dt><dd>IAAC Main Hall, Barcelona</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Hosted by</dt><dd>NODE Engineering Club</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <figure class="mission-cover">
        <img src="/images/missions/forum/forum-iaac-weekly.jpg" alt="Marine Technology and Innovation Forum 2026 banner: 21 May, 18:30 at IAAC Main Hall, with partner logos">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission-section">
    <div class="mission-section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">The forum</div>
      <p class="mission-text">Our first event, the Marine Technology &amp; Innovation Forum, was hosted at IAAC Barcelona. It was an evening that brought together team members, prospective recruits, partners and industry professionals to share and discuss state-of-the-art technologies in robotics and marine research.</p>
      <p class="mission-text">IAAC members opened the evening by highlighting their interest in advancing prototyping and digital fabrication through their support of NODE. NODE then presented their vessel, ASKET, along with its latest updates ahead of the Njord Competition in Trondheim in 2026. Open Cosmos shared their latest satellite technology for marine monitoring with high-resolution imagery. Finally, Cerulean Sonar presented their work on affordable, high-quality sensing technologies. They also explained why they support NODE: student-led initiatives help advance research on their products.</p>
      <p class="mission-text">Throughout the event, many interesting conversations sparked and connections were made that will help strengthen our work in the field and share it more widely.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

